{"task_id": "HumanEval/17", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef parse_music(music_string: str) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\" Input to this function is a string representing musical notes in a special ASCII format.\n    Your task is to parse this string and return list of integers corresponding to how many beats does each\n    not last.\n\n    Here is a legend:\n    'o' - whole note, lasts four beats\n    'o|' - half note, lasts two beats\n    '.|' - quater note, lasts one beat\n\n    >>> parse_music('o o| .| o| o| .| .| .| .| o o')\n    [4, 2, 1, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 4, 4]\n    \"\"\"\n    # Define the mapping from note string representation to its beat duration.\n    NOTE_MAPPINGS = {\n        'o': 4,    # whole note\n        'o|': 2,   # half note\n        '.|': 1    # quarter note\n    }\n\n    # Split the input string by spaces to get individual note tokens.\n    note_tokens = music_string.split(' ')\n    beat_durations: List[int] = []\n\n    for token in note_tokens:\n        if not token:  # Skip any empty strings resulting from multiple spaces.\n            continue\n        # Look up the beat duration for the token and append it to the results.\n        # If a token is not in NOTE_MAPPINGS, it will raise a KeyError,\n        # which acts as the 'InvalidNoteError' in this simplified,\n        # self-contained function.\n        beats = NOTE_MAPPINGS[token]\n        beat_durations.append(beats)\n\n    return beat_durations\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/19", "solution": "def sort_numbers(numbers: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\" Input is a space-delimited string of numberals from 'zero' to 'nine'.\n    Return the string with numbers sorted from smallest to largest\n    \"\"\"\n    number_word_to_int_map = {\n        'zero': 0, 'one': 1, 'two': 2, 'three': 3, 'four': 4,\n        'five': 5, 'six': 6, 'seven': 7, 'eight': 8, 'nine': 9\n    }\n    int_to_number_word_map = {\n        0: 'zero', 1: 'one', 2: 'two', 3: 'three', 4: 'four',\n        5: 'five', 6: 'six', 7: 'seven', 8: 'eight', 9: 'nine'\n    }\n\n    if not numbers.strip():\n        return ''\n\n    word_list = numbers.split(' ')\n\n    # Convert words to integers\n    int_list = [number_word_to_int_map[word] for word in word_list]\n\n    # Sort integers\n    int_list.sort()\n\n    # Convert sorted integers back to words\n    sorted_word_list = [int_to_number_word_map[num] for num in int_list]\n\n    return ' '.join(sorted_word_list)"}
