{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "```python\ndef fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence.  Do not use recursion.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n    14\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize the last four values for n=0, 1, 2, 3\n    # a = fib4(i-4), b = fib4(i-3), c = fib4(i-2), d = fib4(i-1)\n    a, b, c, d = 0, 0, 2, 0\n\n    # Iterate from n=4 up to the desired n\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib = a + b + c + d\n        a = b\n        b = c\n        c = d\n        d = next_fib\n\n    return d\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "def median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(l, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    if not l:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n\n    # Validate elements are numeric\n    for item in l:\n        if not isinstance(item, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(\"List elements must be numbers (int or float).\")\n\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_l)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # Odd number of elements\n        return sorted_l[n // 2]\n    else:\n        # Even number of elements\n        mid1 = sorted_l[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_l[n // 2]\n        return (mid1 + mid2) / 2.0```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/49", "solution": "```python\ndef modp(n: int, p: int):\n    \"\"\"Return 2^n modulo p using modular exponentiation by squaring.\n    This function efficiently calculates (2^n) % p, handling large n without overflow.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1 % p\n\n    result = 1\n    base = 2 % p\n\n    while n > 0:\n        if n % 2 == 1:\n            result = (result * base) % p\n        base = (base * base) % p\n        n //= 2\n    return result\n```"}
