{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "```python\ndef decode_shift(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Decodes a string by shifting each alphabetic character back by 5 positions.\n    Non-alphabetic characters remain unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for ch in s:\n        if 'a' <= ch <= 'z':\n            # Shift lowercase character back by 5, wrapping around 'a' to 'z'\n            start = ord('a')\n            decoded_char_code = start + (ord(ch) - start - 5) % 26\n            result.append(chr(decoded_char_code))\n        elif 'A' <= ch <= 'Z':\n            # Shift uppercase character back by 5, wrapping around 'A' to 'Z'\n            start = ord('A')\n            decoded_char_code = start + (ord(ch) - start - 5) % 26\n            result.append(chr(decoded_char_code))\n        else:\n            # Non-alphabetic characters remain unchanged\n            result.append(ch)\n    return \"\".join(result)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/57", "solution": "```python\ndef monotonic(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return True is list elements are monotonically increasing or decreasing.\"\"\"\n    if len(l) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # Check if the list is monotonically increasing (non-decreasing)\n    is_increasing = True\n    for i in range(1, len(l)):\n        if l[i] < l[i-1]:\n            is_increasing = False\n            break\n\n    # Check if the list is monotonically decreasing (non-increasing)\n    is_decreasing = True\n    for i in range(1, len(l)):\n        if l[i] > l[i-1]:\n            is_decreasing = False\n            break\n\n    return is_increasing or is_decreasing\n```"}
