{"task_id": "HumanEval/93", "solution": "```python\nVOWELS_LOWER = \"aeiou\"\nVOWELS_UPPER = \"AEIOU\"\nALPHABET_LOWER = \"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\"\nALPHABET_UPPER = \"ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ\"\n\ndef _is_vowel(char: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a character is an English vowel.\"\"\"\n    return char in VOWELS_LOWER or char in VOWELS_UPPER\n\ndef _get_shifted_char(char: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Shifts an English alphabet letter two places forward, with wrap-around.\"\"\"\n    if char.islower():\n        idx = ALPHABET_LOWER.find(char)\n        if idx != -1:\n            return ALPHABET_LOWER[(idx + 2) % len(ALPHABET_LOWER)]\n    elif char.isupper():\n        idx = ALPHABET_UPPER.find(char)\n        if idx != -1:\n            return ALPHABET_UPPER[(idx + 2) % len(ALPHABET_UPPER)]\n    return char\n\ndef _swap_char_case(char: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Swaps the case of a character if it's a letter.\"\"\"\n    return char.swapcase()\n\ndef encode(message):\n    \"\"\"\n    Encodes a message by swapping letter cases and shifting vowels two places forward.\n    Non-alphabetic characters remain unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    encoded_chars = []\n    for char in message:\n        if char.isalpha():\n            if _is_vowel(char):\n                shifted_char = _get_shifted_char(char)\n                encoded_chars.append(_swap_char_case(shifted_char))\n            else:\n                encoded_chars.append(_swap_char_case(char))\n        else:\n            encoded_chars.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(encoded_chars)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/95", "solution": "```python\ndef check_dict_case(dict):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a dictionary, return True if all keys are strings in lower\n    case or all keys are strings in upper case, else return False.\n    The function should return False is the given dictionary is empty.\n    Examples:\n    check_dict_case({\"a\":\"apple\", \"b\":\"banana\"}) should return True.\n    check_dict_case({\"a\":\"apple\", \"A\":\"banana\", \"B\":\"banana\"}) should return False.\n    check_dict_case({\"a\":\"apple\", 8:\"banana\", \"a\":\"apple\"}) should return False.\n    check_dict_case({\"Name\":\"John\", \"Age\":\"36\", \"City\":\"Houston\"}) should return False.\n    check_dict_case({\"STATE\":\"NC\", \"ZIP\":\"12345\" }) should return True.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not dict:\n        return False\n\n    keys = list(dict.keys())\n\n    # Ensure all keys are strings.\n    if not all(isinstance(key, str) for key in keys):\n        return False\n\n    # Check if all string keys are lowercase.\n    all_lower = all(key == key.lower() for key in keys)\n    if all_lower:\n        return True\n\n    # Check if all string keys are uppercase.\n    all_upper = all(key == key.upper() for key in keys)\n    if all_upper:\n        return True\n\n    # If neither condition is met, keys are mixed case or not consistently cased.\n    return False\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/96", "solution": "```python\ndef count_up_to(n):\n    \"\"\"Implement a function that takes a non-negative integer and returns an array of the first n\n    integers that are prime numbers and less than n.\n    for example:\n    count_up_to(5) => [2,3]\n    count_up_to(11) => [2,3,5,7]\n    count_up_to(0) => []\n    count_up_to(20) => [2,3,5,7,11,13,17,19]\n    count_up_to(1) => []\n    count_up_to(18) => [2,3,5,7,11,13,17]\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def is_prime(num):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a given number is prime.\"\"\"\n        if num < 2:\n            return False\n        for i in range(2, int(num**0.5) + 1):\n            if num % i == 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    if n <= 2:\n        return []\n\n    primes = []\n    for num in range(2, n):\n        if is_prime(num):\n            primes.append(num)\n    return primes\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/98", "solution": "```python\ndef count_upper(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a string s, count the number of uppercase vowels in even indices.\n\n    For example:\n    count_upper('aBCdEf') returns 1\n    count_upper('abcdefg') returns 0\n    count_upper('dBBE') returns 0\n    \"\"\"\n    UPPERCASE_VOWELS = {'A', 'E', 'I', 'O', 'U'}\n    count = 0\n    for i, char in enumerate(s):\n        if i % 2 == 0 and char in UPPERCASE_VOWELS:\n            count += 1\n    return count\n```"}
